      "created_at": "2025-02-24T12:26:51Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-02-24T12:26:51Z",
      "body": "> using Py_UNUSED(ignored) is useless, it doesn't tell you at first glance whether it's a NOARGS or a ONEARG/VARARGS method while Py_UNUSED(dummy), Py_UNUSED(arg) and Py_UNUSED(args) would tell you more\r\n\r\nFWIW, I'm skeptical here -- I don't think we can make it *reliably* tell you more. But, if it doesn't matter, why not use your suggestions.\r\n",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
